          %p While this numbering is very nice for augmented simplicial sets, it is not standard, and it can be easily misunderstood, so we do not use it in this article.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Anything that applies to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            should also apply to augmented simplicial sets, if one properly takes care of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+thinking"} negative thinking
            necessary to deal with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{-1}
          %p
            Every augmented simplicial set has an underlying unaugmented simplicial set found by forgetting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{-1}
            (and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^{-1}_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            augmented simplicial set by augmentation over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X)
            (the set of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofree+object"} cofree
            augmented simplicial set by augmentation over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
